think Read Kyri + Radiant Style to write in voice, then REMEMBER (live edge), REDS, and the top of the session-log index to pick up the running thread. Standfast clear -- every red in crux/REDS.md is CLOSED, released, or resting as custody-gated errata (#75, a deep-debride gate that is Keaton's hand). No open agent-closable red, so constructive work is licensed.
think Lindy-first crux-first: the Microkernel double-seat leads by Lindy yet its only ungated move is study, so the live green edge is Season G open-media. The newest log (gaussian) named its own siblings to grow next: sharpen (the image minus its own blur), drop shadow, frosted panel. Sharpen is the crux -- it owns genuinely NEW pixel math (the signed high-pass difference added back with a clamp), where drop shadow and frosted panel are pure compositions of blur + compose that already stand.
think Built image/sharpen.rye: the classic unsharp mask, clamp(orig + amount * (orig - gaussian_blur)) per channel. amount is a PERCENT over sharpen_amount_scale (100) so a designer reads it plainly (0 identity, 100 full, 200 double); i32 intermediate truncated toward zero so bright/dark overshoot stay symmetric and a sharpen is deterministic; clamp lands an overshoot on a rail, never a wrap. Stands on gaussian.gaussian_blur (which stands on blur.box_blur) + qoi -- one new operation, no hidden blur or blend.
think One honest fix on the first metal run: the "flat interior holds" check used an 8px row where a radius-2 3-pass Gaussian's reach touched index 0, so it moved. Widened to a 16px row so the interior pixel lies beyond the blur's reach -- the honest scope of the claim, not a loosened assert. GREEN after: amount 0 and radius 0 both the identity byte-for-byte; the module equals a hand-composed unsharp mask byte-for-byte (composition crux); a flat field gains nothing even at max amount; the EDGE CRUX -- a midtone step 64->192 gains an under/overshoot halo (dark side below 64, bright side above 192, contrast expands past 128, flat interior held); a strong amount clamps to 0/255 with no wrap; alpha sharpened like any channel; QOI round-trip; three refusals by name; determinism.
obs Discipline: tools/sharpen_witness.rish uses native `assert selftest.out contains` (REDS #85/#76 convention, never printf|grep). tame_style_check bans clean (my file carries full asserts, not in the zero-assert ratchet), width-check clean, ASCII clean, living-docs advisory-only, living-card ASCII GREEN after the REMEMBER edit. README grows a Crispen summary bullet + a full sharpen.rye entry; REMEMBER's live edge prepends sharpen as the newest rung, single-stranded onto the gaussian chain.
